justification:"Airy phases have modulus one. Strong continuity follows by convergence on any fixed finite set of modes, with the remaining square-summable tails bounded uniformly by four times the original tail. For Dinv, <k>^2/k^2<=2 when k!=0; deleting the zero coefficient cannot increase a Fourier norm. For multiplication, <k>^r<=C_r(<l>^r+<k-l>^r) bounds the weighted convolution by two ell^2-ell^1 convolutions. Their ell^2 norms are bounded by the product of the respective sequence norms, by the triangle inequality applied to translated sequences. Cauchy-Schwarz gives ||hat h||_ell^1<= (sum <k>^(-2r))^(1/2)||h||_(H^r); the series converges for r>1/2. This proves the asserted bilinear continuity, first on polynomials and then by density. Composition in the endpoint formula, subtraction of the initial endpoint, and the inclusion to H^agamma prove continuity as used in S003."
